{#- embed-panel.njk — the view switch, and everything the embed needs

   AT THE TOP, and it REPLACES the page's own rendering rather than sitting
   beside it. On Support the console already draws goal cards; showing the
   widget underneath would put two of nearly the same thing on one screen and
   leave you comparing them. So this is a view switch: Edit, or As embedded.

   That also answers "a toggle to hide the visualiser and just edit the data" —
   it is the same control, read the other way round.

   The caller sets `embedWidget` to "roadmap" or "goal". There is no widget
   picker: the page has already chosen.  -#}

<div class="emb-bar" data-embed-panel data-widget="{{ embedWidget }}" hidden>

  {#- Two buttons, not a checkbox: this chooses between two views, and a tick
     box would imply the second is an addition to the first. -#}
  <div class="emb-views" role="tablist" aria-label="View">
    <button type="button" class="emb-view is-on" role="tab" aria-selected="true"
            data-emb="viewEdit" data-i18n="emb.viewEdit">Edit</button>
    <button type="button" class="emb-view" role="tab" aria-selected="false"
            data-emb="viewEmbed" data-i18n="emb.viewEmbed">As embedded</button>
  </div>

  {#- The live state, always visible, because "is this on someone else's site
     right now" is the question you actually have while looking at either
     view. -#}
  <span class="emb-state" data-emb="state"></span>
</div>

<section class="emb-panel" data-emb="panel" hidden>

  <p class="emb-lede" data-i18n="{{ 'emb.ledeRoadmap' if embedWidget == 'roadmap' else 'emb.ledeGoal' }}">
    {% if embedWidget == "roadmap" %}
      This is exactly what a sending church or a supporter sees when they put
      your roadmap on their own site.
    {% else %}
      This is exactly what a sending church or a supporter sees when they put
      your giving progress on their own site.
    {% endif %}
  </p>

  {#- The widget itself, first and large. Everything under it is about it. -#}
  <div class="emb-stage">
    <iframe data-emb="frame" title="Embed preview" sandbox="allow-scripts"></iframe>
  </div>

  <div class="emb-controls">
    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.accent">Accent</span>
      <span class="emb-colour">
        <input type="color" data-emb="accent" value="#6D4AFF">
        <input type="text" data-emb="accentHex" class="emb-hex" maxlength="7"
               spellcheck="false" aria-label="Accent colour hex">
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.theme">Background</span>
      <select data-emb="theme">
        <option value="auto" data-i18n="emb.auto">Match their page</option>
        <option value="light" data-i18n="emb.light">Always light</option>
        <option value="dark" data-i18n="emb.dark">Always dark</option>
      </select>
    </label>

    <label class="emb-field">
      <span data-i18n="emb.lang">Language</span>
      <select data-emb="lang"></select>
    </label>

  </div>

  <p class="emb-shared" data-i18n="emb.sharedNote">
    Colours are shared by every widget this ministry publishes. The language
    belongs to this snippet only.
  </p>

  {#- THE PUBLICATION DECISION, on its own and worded as what it does rather
     than as a setting name. Everything above works whether this is on or off,
     because you should be able to look before you decide. -#}
  <div class="emb-publish">
    <div class="emb-publish-text">
      <h4 data-i18n="emb.shareTitle">Let other websites show this</h4>
      <p data-emb="shareDesc" data-i18n="emb.shareOff">
        Nobody can use the code below yet. Turn this on and the address starts
        answering — until then it returns nothing at all, not even an error
        saying you exist.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="emb-publish-ctl">
      <button type="button" class="switch" role="switch" aria-checked="false" data-emb="on">
        <span class="switch-track"><span class="switch-state" data-emb="onState">Off</span><span class="switch-knob"></span></span>
      </button>
      <p class="rolegate" data-emb="notAdmin" hidden data-i18n="emb.adminOnly">
        An administrator changes this.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  {#- TWO THINGS TO COPY, and they are for different people.

     The snippet is for whoever runs a website and wants the picture. The data
     address is for whoever is building something of their own and wants the
     numbers — a designer with their own layout, a church intranet, a spread-
     sheet. Offering only the snippet sends the second group looking for an
     API that is already there.  -#}
  <div class="emb-copies">
    <div class="emb-copy">
      <div class="emb-copy-head">
        <h4 data-i18n="emb.snippetTitle">The code to paste</h4>
        <p data-i18n="emb.snippetDesc">For anyone who just wants the picture on their page.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="emb-codewrap">
        <pre class="emb-code" data-emb="code"></pre>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" data-emb="copyCode" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="emb-copy">
      <div class="emb-copy-head">
        <h4 data-i18n="emb.apiTitle">The data behind it</h4>
        <p data-i18n="emb.apiDesc">For anyone building their own design. Plain JSON, same numbers, no key needed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="emb-codewrap">
        <pre class="emb-code" data-emb="api"></pre>
        <button type="button" class="ghost-btn" data-emb="copyApi" data-i18n="common.copy">Copy</button>
      </div>
      {#- The written guide. Increasingly the person building against this will
         hand both to an assistant, and the payload alone cannot say which
         fields grow, that money is in minor units, or that a null date is
         normal. -#}
      <a class="emb-guide" data-emb="guide" download>
        <span data-i18n="emb.guide">Download the developer guide</span>
        <span class="emb-guide-sub" data-i18n="emb.guideSub">Markdown — how to read the data, and how to keep working when goals or milestones are added.</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>
